    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/San-Antonio-TX/Financial-Aid-Advisor-II_R-096743-1": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Advisor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Financial Aid Advisor II Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Enrollment Management Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description This position, under the supervision of the Assistant Director in Financial Aid, will provide student-focused service and guidance regarding student aid programs, educational funding options, and the financial aid application process. The person employed in this position will be able to comprehend, interpret, and apply federal and state regulations and university policies related to financial aid and be able to regularly exercise professional judgment. This position will ensure the compliance of current and new procedures and/or processes are followed and adhered to in regard to federal, state, and institutional policies while making financial aid for students readily attainable and as efficient as possible. In addition, the position will be responsible for ensuring that excellent customer service is provided to students within the Enrollment Service Center, allowing for a one stop customer service opportunity. This position normally works Monday-Friday; 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. May work beyond normal office hours to include evenings, weekends, and peak time periods. Responsibilities: Provides student financial aid counseling in the Enrollment Service Center. This includes meeting with students, answering phone calls, and assisting enrollment service advisors. Facilitates student financial aid file review to assist students and families. Duties include assisting students in navigating financial aid applications and reviewing financial aid awards to ensure accuracy and compliance with institutional and governmental guidelines. Understand, interpret, and effectively communicate details of current federal, state, and institutional policies, procedures, and regulations pertaining to financial aid, student employment, and scholarships. Attains and maintains knowledge of major programs and establishes administrative procedures to ensure the proper processing and documentation of awards in accordance with federal and state laws, regulations, and university policies. Assists the associate directors in revising and/or approving the awarding of financial aid through the specific controls of program policy and guidelines. Makes adjustments if necessary. Processes Satisfactory Academic Progress appeals and makes decisions regarding the validity of these appeals and any other steps the student must take to satisfy a judgment rendered to reestablish eligibility for financial aid or scholarships in accordance with established university Satisfactory Academic Progress (SAP) policy. Reviews and processes Professional Judgment. Assists associate directors with internal audit controls. Participate in committees such as Audit, Forms, PPM/SOP, Technology, Testing, Training/Professional Development, SAP, and Social/Retreat in the Office of Financial Aid and Scholarships. Assists with monitoring the over-award resolution process. Resolves over-award problems within Banner based on the student receiving additional resources (scholarships and outside resources) after processing of the initial award package. Develops effective working relationships with appropriate personnel in administrative/academic support offices (e.g., Admissions, Registrar’s Office, Student Business Services, etc.) Assists with conducting on and off campus presentations and seminars for students (high school, prospective, admitted, and current) and possibly for professional development training. Events include, but are not limited to Future Jaguar Day and Paying for College. May work at resource tables as requested by a group from TAMUSA, prospective student groups, and others. Maintains punctual attendance in accordance with the defined office schedule, and/or as assigned, to facilitate excellent customer service and accurate and timely completion of all components of financial aid administration, e.g., verification, awarding, loan certification, etc. Completes assigned goals, tasks, and projects in an accurate and timely manner. Performs other duties as assigned. This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree or higher in related field. One (1) year of related experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Proficient with common software applications (e.g. Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint)and spreadsheet applications. Knowledge of financial aid systems such as Banner. Federal Student Financial Aid experience at a previous educational institution. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others, both internal and external constituents. Oral and written communication skills. Well-developed public presentation skills. Self -starter, exercising initiative. Detail and goal oriented. Ability to organize and make decisions. Customer Service skills. Ability to work individually or as a team. Ability to relate well with a students. Other Requirements: Requires some evening and weekend work. Applicant   Instructions:     Please make sure to provide the following documents:    Cover Letter   Resume   / CV     Professional References     For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:    http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html   ​     Summary of Employee Benefits:     www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf     Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.    Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to   submitting   the application. Once   the   application is   submitted , no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents   to   your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.     In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.    All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
    },
    "https://tamus.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/San-Antonio-TX/Enrollment-Services-Advisor-II_R-096750": {
      "title": "Enrollment Services Advisor II",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-02\nPosted: Posted 3 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title Enrollment Services Advisor II Agency Texas A&M University - San Antonio Department Welcome Center Proposed Minimum Salary Commensurate Job Location San Antonio, Texas Job Type Staff Job Description The Enrollment Services Advisor II, under general supervision, provides customer service to students, faculty, and staff through various communication channels. Offers information regarding University services and information related to admissions, academics, registration procedures, advising services, residency, transcripts, academic programs, and financial aid. Provides training and leadership to other staff and student workers. Responsibilities: Provides customer service to students, faculty, and staff who phone in and email inquiries. Advises students and helps in the decision-making process regarding financial aid and admission status for new and current students. Prepares and maintains database with information sent to prospective students and ensures that follow-up contact is made with students who have expressed interest in the University. Oversees daily customer flow of the Enrollment Services Center walk-in visits and inbound calls; monitors call queues and in person queues. Maintains database of inbound and outbound call communication results to prospective students regarding applying for admission and registration. Assists Director and Assistant Director in monitoring departmental tracking and reporting using various reporting mechanisms including but not limited to: CRM (Element451), Banner, CISCO, QLess, JIRA. Resolves concerns of students and issues related to the enrollment process. Review and update administrative processes and procedures. Assists in overseeing the Student ID Card operation in maintaining the software and equipment needed to make ID cards for all students, staff, and faculty. Informs current business processes to ensure students receive proper information and assistance in enrollment. Provides customer service to students, faculty, and staff on phone and email inquiries. May actively recruit and help in the decision-making processes of financial aid and scheduling for new and current students. Assist the Director and Assistant Director in planning, implementing, and developing events and outreach programs related to recruitment and financial aid, such as Paying For College events and Future Jaguar Day. Conducts presentations and informational sessions on admissions requirements and programs. Some travel is required to attend special recruitment events and engagements. Prepares documents and correspondence for new students, including but not limited to acceptance letters and new student information packets. Remove student enrollment holds and use critical decisionmaking skills to ensure students matriculate from acceptance to enrollment. Participate in New Student Orientation events and make decisions to assist students in the enrollment process, including, but not limited to: removal of enrollment holds, awarding of financial aid, and scholarships. Maintains knowledge of current state, federal, and institutional policies and procedures.   This document represents the major duties, responsibilities, and authorities of this job, and is not intended to be a complete list of all tasks and functions. Other duties may be assigned. Required Education and Experience: Bachelor’s degree or higher in related field. Two (2) years of related experience. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of word processing, spreadsheet, and database applications. Ability to multitask and work cooperatively with others. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to multitask and work both independently and as a team. Ability to organize and make decisions. Ability to relate well with a multicultural student population. Ability to comprehend and communicate technical information effectively and diplomatically. Ability to convey customer service skills, interpersonal skills, and be detail-oriented. Licensing / Professional Certification: None. Physical Requirements: None. The physical demands described here are representative of those that must be met by an employee to successfully perform the essential functions of this job. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions.   Supervision of Others: This position may require some supervision. Other Requirements: Work beyond normal office hours and/or work on weekends.   Applicant Requirement Instructions:     Please make sure to provide the following documents:    Cover Letter   Resume / CV   Professional References     For detailed instructions on how to apply for any position on our website, please use the following link:    http://www.tamusa.edu/humanresources/job-opportunities/index.html ​       Summary of Employee Benefits:     www.tamusa.edu/human-resources/documents/Summary-of-Employees-Benefits1.pdf       Texas A&M University-San Antonio values community engagement and encourages applicants who are committed to advancing the well-being and prosperity of our communities.    Please ensure that all required documents are uploaded prior to submitting the application. Once the application is submitted , no changes or revisions can be made.  If you have issues with adding documents to your application, please contact HR at 210-784-2058.       In compliance with ADA, if accommodations are needed for the application process, please contact HR at (210) 784-2058.    All positions are security-sensitive. Applicants are subject to a criminal history investigation, and employment is contingent upon the institution’s verification of credentials and/or other information required by the institution’s procedures, including the completion of the criminal history check. Equal Opportunity/Veterans/Disability Employer."
